    choiceDetail: You know too many cars on the road cause traffic congestion, so
      you relocate your second car on high risk days.
  longerTitle: Multi-Car Household
  description: 'Households with multiple cars face a dilemma during evacuations.
    Some wish to keep all their vehicles with them when they evacuate. It is very
    important to consider the consequences of such choices. Splitting the family
    into multiple vehicles during an evacuation increases risks of being separated,
    as well as causing additional congestion during evacuation. If it is important
    to keep both vehicles, consider relocating one of them to a safe place on red
    flag days to keep yourselves and your belongings safe.

'
